Hi,

I've uploaded the new files in the results of a bulk build for
NetBSD/alpha 4.0_BETA to

   ftp://ftp.NetBSD.org/pub/pkgsrc/packages-2006Q3/NetBSD-4.0/alpha/

A total of 2.0GB of packages were uploaded.  Among the packages
available in new versions are: abiword, amavisd-new, ap2-php5,
bugzilla, clamav, cups, firefox, foomatic-filters, gtexinfo,
guile-gtk, ingo, libarchive, milter-greylist, mutt, mysql-client,
mysql-server, openssh, php (4 & 5), phpmyadmin, png, postgres*,
proftpd, qt3, ruby18-base, screen, squid, tcl-postgresql74,
thunderbird, and wireshark.

The source tree this was built from was updated November 21.

As indicated above, the build was done on a machine running
NetBSD 4.0_BETA, so these packages are not compatible with
installations using packages from before we switched to gcc 4.

This is the last build of pkgsrc-2006Q3 for this OS/arch
combination; the build host will next build packages from the
pkgsrc-2006Q4 branch.

Regards,

- H=E5vard


